      "relation": "implemented-in"
    }
  ],
  "level_notes": {
    "1": "No external standard: The Racket Reference (level 1) is normative alongside the implementation; The Racket Guide is the official tutorial (level 2). Key design papers (scope sets, compilable macros, Typed Scheme) define core mechanisms.",
    "0": "racket/racket contains Racket CS (default since 8.0; runtime \"rumble\" layer on Chez Scheme, expander/io/thread layers written in Racket) and the legacy BC C runtime."
